# The turso sqlite database token
TURSO_DB_TOKEN=eyJ...
# The libsql connection URL for the Turso database (tursodb engine, required for
# BEGIN CONCURRENT / MVCC support)
TURSO_DB_URL=libsql://painting-local-legoguy.aws-us-east-2.turso.io

# The signing keyset: an ordered, comma-separated list of <kid>:<key>
# entries. The FIRST entry is the primary — everything new (guest session
# cookies today; WebAuthn challenges, merge tokens, and transfer codes in
# later phases) is signed under it via HKDF-derived, purpose-specific
# subkeys. Every entry is tried when verifying, so listing more than one lets
# an old key keep validating tokens through a rotation — see
# docs/signing-key-rotation.md for the full procedure.
#
# Each <kid> is a short opaque id matching /^[a-z0-9]{1,16}$/ (no meaning
# beyond "which key" — e.g. "k1", "k2"). Each <key> is exactly 32 random
# bytes, base64url-encoded (no TextEncoder-over-a-string business — generate
# real key material):
#     openssl rand -base64 32 | tr '+/' '-_' | tr -d '='
PAINTING_KEYS=k1:replace-with-a-generated-base64url-32-byte-key

# Unlike PAINTING_KEYS, each Deno Deploy context (Production/Preview/Local)
# should get its OWN keyset — a preview deployment must never be able to
# mint a token production honours. Use scripts/set-deploy-env.ts to set a
# different PAINTING_KEYS value per context (see
# docs/deno-deploy-env-vars.md); do not use `deno deploy env add`, which
# forces one value across every context.

# Legacy-verification-only, pre-keyset guest-cookie secrets (Phase 0). Kept
# ONLY so guests still carrying a v1/v2 cookie verify and get transparently
# re-issued as v3 under PAINTING_KEYS above — nothing signs with these
# anymore. Safe to unset once GUEST_SESSION_SECRET has been out of use for
# longer than the guest cookie's 400-day max-age; slated for removal.
GUEST_SESSION_SECRET=replace-with-at-least-32-random-bytes
GUEST_SESSION_SECRET_PREVIOUS=replace-with-the-previous-secret-during-rotation

# Set to 1 only for local development (deno task dev sets this automatically).
# Serves client/shared/css assets unhashed with no-store, skips the import-map
# and HTML-rewrite caching, so editing a file is visible on the next request
# with no restart. Leave unset in every deployed context (Production, Preview,
# Build) so they get content-hashed, immutably-cached assets instead.
PAINTING_DEV=1

# WebAuthn (passkey) relying party config. A credential is bound forever to
# the RP ID it was registered under, so this must be the canonical
# registrable domain and must NEVER change once real accounts exist — see
# RELATED-ORIGIN-REQUESTS.md for the full rationale. Every account route
# 501s if these are unset, or if the request's Origin header isn't in
# WEBAUTHN_ORIGINS, so previews stay fully testable for guest flows while
# account creation only works on the canonical domain (or localhost, which
# is a WebAuthn secure context by spec — useful for local dev only).
WEBAUTHN_RP_ID=localhost
WEBAUTHN_ORIGINS=http://localhost:8000

# Turso platform (organization) management API token — used by the ephemeral
# database suite and environment database tools. Those tools resolve a target
# database and mint a transient in-process connection token, so .env does not
# need credentials for every deployment database. Never used by the app.
TURSO_API_KEY=eyJ...
TURSO_ORG_SLUG=legoguy

# Deno Deploy personal access token — only needed to run scripts/set-deploy-env.ts,
# which sets per-context (Production/Preview/Build/Local) env vars on the
# deployed app. Never used by the app itself. See docs/deno-deploy-env-vars.md.
DENO_DEPLOY_TOKEN=ddp_...
